@@ -121,0 +122,2 @@ ## Construction Demand Closure
+Parent lookahead joins pending requests by their canonical parent field within one analysis and combines checked and unchecked requirements independently. Each join combines exact keys with the same applicability set and recursively compacts their nested selections, preserving argument tuples, inherited guards, and the separate root type-check condition. Shared interface selections remain shared; concrete specialization and overlapping abstract/concrete alternatives are merged when the occurrence's runtime type is known. Shared resolver/checker templates therefore contribute one requirement per semantic destination and provenance instead of retaining copies for every dependency path. Immutable forest normalization is memoized only within that lookahead computation; no occurrence values or runtime bindings are cached. Left-to-right alternative order remains intact, and analyses affected by a recursion cut remain ineligible for template memoization. This bounds the repeated diamond contributions, not the cost of arbitrary distinct requirement sets or condition graphs.
+
